{"title":"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two diagonals are drawn in the trapezoid\nforming four triangles. The areas of two of the\ntriangles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as shown. What is the total\narea of the trapezoid?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/2/402684b2f1013e5842db62e6b3d685aa5698aec9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(20,0)--(2,4)--(14,4)--(0,0),black); draw((0,0)--(2,4)--(14,4)--(20,0),black); MP(&quot;25&quot;,(9,.25),N);MP(&quot;9&quot;,(9,2.25),N); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"52\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By definition of a trapezoid, the two bases are parallel. Because the intersecting lines are transversals of the two parallel lines, we know that the two triangles with known areas are similar by angle-angle-angle similarity. Noticing that the areas of the triangles are square numbers, we know that the base of the triangle must be 2 times an integer and that that integer squared is the area of the triangle. We find that the bases are 6 and 10 and the heights are 3 and 5. Using that formula for the area of a trapezoid, we find that the area of the trapezoid is ((6+10)/2)*(5+3) and this is 8*8, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/0/330f919429e279b05cb9cd753567d7b6e0bb5218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II\">2009 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://uncmathcontest.wordpress.com/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title